==English==

===Etymology===
From the [[Anglo-Norman French]] legal phrase [[hu e cri]].

===Noun phrase===
{{wikipedia}}
'''[[hue]] and [[cry]]'''
#(''formerly'') the [[public]] [[pursuit]] of a [[felon]]; accompanied by [[shout]]s to warn others to [[give chase]]
#(''by extension'') a [[loud]] and [[persistent]] public [[clamour]]; especially one of [[protest]] or making some [[demand]]

